# Fractured Identity: "Exile target nonland permanent." A land is not a legal target (refused beside the Ornithopter that
# is), and the permanent's controller is not special to the target: Bot1 exiles its own Ornithopter and "each player other
# than its controller" is Bot2, who creates the token copy. Bot1 gets nothing back.

[Bot1 Deck]
Fractured Identity
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Ornithopter
Island
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
[Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Hand.Fractured Identity.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Island)
Bot1.Hand.Fractured Identity.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Exile = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Mox Pearl; Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Types = Artifact; Creature
